YAFAP Morgan Le Fay -Wiz-Elf-Fem-Cha

I played on and off for about about a year and a half, essentially
unspoiled.So I figured out quite a few things on my own, the hard
way. For instance I learned about cheap plastic imitations of
the Amulet of Yendor when i found a wand of wishing on level 1.
Anyway last summer I started to read spoilers on nethack and have
since improved my play. I've had some close calls. I even escaped
the dungeon in celestial disgrace once.

This is the story of my first ascension which was pretty much a
marathon for me. I hardly even ate or slept, or showered for that
mater, in the roughly two days I played this game. Since I spent
so much time playing under bodily stress, I made quite a few very
silly mistakes that could have cost me my ascension. Initially, I
just wanted to try a silly strategy, dig for victory. Thus an
elven wizard is a nice choice. My first level had a chaotic alter,
which is nice but useless without food. The next level had a
branch for the mine which is great luck if one wants to dig for
victory. But after checking the first level of the mines for some
yummy gnome corpses and a pick axe I had a change of heart.
Why not use the alter on the 1st level to get my magicbane?

But first I need food so I might as well delve down to Sokoban.So
with my kitten I descended down the main dungeon branch exploring
each level enough to know if it was the Oracle or not. Once at a
high enough level, I cast haste self as often until I could raise
my skill level. I I found quite a bit of gold and 3 shops on the
way down. I found a spellbook of confuse monster in a shop and
cast that whenever I got the chance. Now I was fast and had very
very red glowing hands. The oracle was very deep and I had
acquired both food and a bag of tricks. With this I gave up and
returned to level one. Eventually, I was granted a magicbane,
just what I wanted. Around this time my housecat went missing,
oh well these things happen.

So I started a stash with a magicbane elbereth and was braver and
dove again towards Sokoban. On the way down team killer bee
nearly wasted me. I was blinded by a yellow light so no elbereth
and got down to 6 hp. I could luckily see most of the bees near
me were immediate. So I decided to break a wand of sleep. This
luckily worked and even killed quite a few of them. I ran quickly
to an upstairs and avoided anything for a while.

After this close call sokoban was a picnic giving me an amulet of
reflection and enough cash to play the protection racket a couple
of times. So I went back to my stash and dropped things off then
dove to minetown. I was very pleased to find a very expensive bag
in the tool shop with the property that it seemed to make my load
lighter when I put things in it. So I bought my bag of holding
fair and square. I also picked up quite a collection of spells
from my local general store. With some luck the alter in minetown
was chaotic, so I didn't feel bad donating to such an
understanding priest. I sacrificed things on the alter and was
gifted the Fire Brand then the Frost Brand. I had an okay
collection of armor, but not anything great. Some stray dog I had
offered a pancake killed a couple guards for some gloves and
studded leather armor. He then got killed himself, oh well
another pet bites the dust.

I found a touchstone on my way down to the mines end. I went back
up and made some water holy to bless it. I used this to ID all my
gems and separate the glass from the valuable. With proficiency
in remove curse I built up I was unafraid of a loadstone and
even picked one up. Luckily it wasn't too heavy of one, or maybe
the workout I had in sokoban buffed up my stats. I also got my
luckstone which I also blessed.

Then I took it upon myself to find as much gold as possible to buy
as much protection as I could. Eventually I ended up killing all
the shopkeepers and even a bunch of Kops just for fun. I found a
neglected magic lamp in one of the deeper shops which I blessed
and got some speed boots. I tried dumping some duplicate rings in
a sink and found my ring of searching and slow digestion. Now what
I really wanted was identify. So back up to my level 1 alter and
sacrificed and prayed until I was crowned. Then more of the same
until I got the spellbook I wanted. It helped that I had found a
spellbook of create monster along the way. An interesting oddity
is my God said the "hark mortal  you need the correct tune", but
never gave it to me.

I eventually IDed all my stuff along with 2 scrolls of genocide,
1 cursed and 1 uncursed. I took out master mind flayers first
cause I just hate the little buggers. Then I reverse genocided
silver dragons after making sure I had a nice elbereth carved in
before. I used some scrolls of enchant armor to harden my
scale mail and fireproof my cloak.

So now my AC was beginning to look quite reasonable.
Intrinsically, I think I was down to about 2. I wanted to
be quite prepared for the quest so I went and took care of Medusa
first with a ring of levitation. I then decided to do the castle
before my quest. I wanted to use the drawbridge to kill a bunch
of monsters using my bungle. Unfortunately, I could not even
get a single mastermind like clue no mater wear I stood or played.
So I blasted the drawbridge with force bolt and proceeded to rain
down Fingers of Death and magic missiles to all that withstood.
Once I killed or destroyed the lot I got my wand of wishing and
some tins of dragon meat, black was the one I really wanted.
I had already found a couple of scrolls of charging so wished for

1) blessed greased rustproof +2 helm of brilliance
2) blessed rustproof +3 stormbringer

3) blessed master key of thievery
4) blessed amulet of life saving
5) blessed spellbook of polymorph

I then was quite confident for my quest and did it easily at about
XP 20.I got the stormbringer for level gain protection against
V and W mainly. I didn't realize it was not +3 or rustproof
till much later.

The rest of my ascension was not too hard but I kick myself over
these 3 huge mistakes:

1) I accidentally vaporized my helm of brilliance with a poorly
checked ?oEA.

2) I accidentally ate my magicbane when polymorphed into a rock
mole!

3) After dancing with a nurse I found on Orcus' level, I used my
towel as a blindfold to see where she went. Then blind and naked
I walked over a cockatrice corpse wasting one of my 10 amulets
of life saving.

I basically polypiled the hell out of things. I once got a saddle
and decided I would ride a dragon out with the amulet in style.
This plan failed when we tried to go upstairs but instead were
teleported next to a black dragon who disintegrated my 5th
dragon steed (saddle and all) and I could not find a saddle for
the rest of the game.

I didn't want to make the same mistake as last time and sacrifice
on the wrong altar. So I made sure the only way I knew how, by
trying to engrave. I unfortunately had to go to all 3 altars
(right to left). Famine also decided to follow me from the middle
area to join Death on the left. This made life fun. Before death
got to my character she had almost 500 hp, but survived
comfortably the lowest she got at any point after the dungeon was
290hp.

Anyway it was a blast. Many thanks to the Dev-Team.

